Each class's members are indented under that class, and the `const value` between the two classes is back at the top level.
== args
input/multi-class.ts
== file input/multi-class.ts
export class A {
  run(): void {}
}

const value = 1;

class B {
  constructor() {}
}
== stdout
input/multi-class.ts (9 lines)
[L1-L3] export class A
  [L2-L2] run(): void
[L5-L5] const value
[L7-L9] class B
  [L8-L8] constructor()
